{
 "id": "P27",
 "kind": "echarts",
 "title": "The same score cutoff audits 0.2% to 12% of clean code",
 "section": "setup",
 "order": 25,
 "caption": "Share of our 500 clean programs each monitor would send to a human if you audited every program scoring 5 or more out of 10. The dashed line is a 2% budget, and the axis is on a log scale. The dial changes the cutoff score.",
 "notes": [
  "One configuration per model, at its default reasoning effort, 0 to 10 scale, comments removed. One clean program is 0.2% of 500, so 0.2% means a single program.",
  "At a cutoff of 5, 10 monitors audit under 2% and 3 audit over it. At a cutoff of 1 the range is 0.6% to 81%.",
  "Setting each monitor's cutoff on clean code instead (P25) puts every monitor on the dashed line by construction, which is what the study does."
 ],
